Greetings.  This is my first post here, although I've been showing my
face in #nethack for a while now (as futilius).

After a post-quest, post-castle priest choked without confirmation on
a tengu corpse, killing a practically guraranteed six-game streak, I
decided to try a conduct game and this was the result.  I ran into a
few close calls, but mostly it wasn't too bad.  I don't usually identify
or bless anything before the castle, anyway (maybe magic lamps and
BoH's).  I did, however, lose survivor and polyitemless (dip-testing
accident), and spent about 10k turns more than necessary.

Vegan-atheist-illiterate poses some interesting challenges.  Vegan
combined with aetheist means intrinsics have to be acquired the hard
way, and an illiterate atheist won't have very good AC.  Bad AC wasn't
much of a problem thanks to the Orb, but intrinsics were tricky.  I got
poison late, and ascended without shock, sleep, or telepathy.

I started the game as I usually would. I killed any dwarf I came across
and hauled all the armor to the minetown general store, finding a +1
dwarvish mithril coat and a pair of +1 iron shoes.  I got the BoH from
soko, and soon noticed I had two different clear potions in the bag that
wouldn't stack with the rest.  I blessed the magic lamp I bought, rubbed
it for the Sceptre of Might, and started making my way down with the
comfort of MR.

The main dungeon had two more treats for me.  One was an ice troll with
a /oD standing over the bones of a poor monk.  The bones pile had a wand
of enlightenment, which I used to identify rings of free action, teleport
control, and poison resistance.  The =oPR didn't come off until I finally
got PR late in Gehennom.  The monk also had the sadly untouchable MKoT,
plus +4 speed boots and +2 leather gloves, both of which I wore to the
end  (I didn't swap my +1 elven cloak for his +4 robe, because I
decided that would push me over the AC I was likely to reach had I not
encountered bones).  The other break was a throne wish, which went to
a +2 helm of telepathy.

At the castle, I wished for SDSM and wrested for a =oSD.  I found
levitation earlier, so that gave me a full Ring Set minus conflict,
which I had from the Sceptre.  The Sceptre is, by the way, one of the
best artifacts to wish for--I don't believe I ever turned conflict off
after the castle.  At this point I was level 15, so I went and did the
quest.

In Gehennom I started off by looking for Vlad.  No fun at all.  The
entrance was in practically the last corridor explored of the five
possible levels.  I put on the "oLS, level-ported to the bottom and
found the VS.  Here I made a terrible mistake and dropped the Orb instead
of the Bell of Opening.  When I finally made my way back to the VS, half
dead from all the monsters summoned by two master liches and flayed out
of my skull, Demogorgon decided to pop in.  Ill, and with 27 HP left,
I teleported Demo and did un uncontrolled level-port, landing at level
18.

Discouraged, I listlessly re-expore the main dungeon while coming up
with a plan.  Somehow wandering all the way back up to the Oracle level,
I noticed an unexplored room with an unidentified scroll on the floor.
I stand over it and TA-DA!, the leather golem turns to flee!  Armed with
the only scroll I would ever use, I went back to Gehennom, mapped out
all the levels on foot, and slayed Demo.  Stepping up the pace, I manage
to kill both Rodney and the High Priest with the same 'trice corpse,
and started to climb.

The mysterious force was bad.  At one point I spent a few hundred turns
getting knokcked back to level 40 from two levels below the VoTD.  Rodney
was curiously sympathetic to my conduct attempt, and didn't even come
back until I was out of Gehennom.  Although I never knew the charges on
my /oD's (never magically identified anything at all, actually), they
lasted me the rest of the game.

The planes were't hard, and the Orb was handy for finding portals, but
on Water I had my second catastrophe when an electric eel drowned me,
using up my only "oLS.  Of course, he still held me after it was used
up, so I zapped him away, and swapped my elven cloak for an oilskin
cloak (stupid, STUPID me.  And it was +2!).  Astral was breezy.  The
first altar was chaotic, so I get out the found HoOA and ascended.  Yay.

